		 Script to measure the performance of your network and router.
		 
		 Please see https://github.com/openwrt/packages/blob/master/net/speedtest-netperf/files/README.md for further information.
		 Tony Ambardar <itugrok@yahoo.com>

	config PACKAGE_speedtestcpp
		tristate "speedtestcpp................................................. SpeedTest++"
		default y if DEFAULT_speedtestcpp
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_libspeedtestcpp
		select PACKAGE_libstdcpp
		select PACKAGE_libc
		help
		 Yet another unofficial speedtest.net client cli interface
		   forked from taganaka's SpeedTest with few improments and
		   lesser depends.
		 https://github.com/oskarirauta/speedtestcpp
		 Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>

	config PACKAGE_spoofer
		tristate "spoofer.............. Measure your ISP's resistance to spoofed IP packets"
		default y if DEFAULT_spoofer
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_libpthread
		select PACKAGE_libopenssl
		select PACKAGE_protobuf-lite
		select PACKAGE_libpcap
		select PACKAGE_libc
		help
		 The spoofer client is part of a system to measure the Internet's
		 resistance to packets with a spoofed (forged) source IP address.
		 
		 This package comes bundled with small certificate files that allow
		 secure communication with the spoofer server without depending on
		 the large ca-certificates package.  But if the server's private
		 certificate ever changes, it will be necessary to either install the
		 ca-certificates package or install an updated version of this package
		 that has a newer bundled certificate.
		 
		 https://spoofer.caida.org/
		 Ken Keys <spoofer-info@caida.org>

	config PACKAGE_sscep
		tristate "sscep...... A Simple SCEP (Simple Certificate Enrollment Protocol) client"
		default y if DEFAULT_sscep
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_libc
		select PACKAGE_libopenssl
		select PACKAGE_openssl-util
		help
		 sscep is a simple SCEP client published by the CertNanny project.
		 
		   It is used to retrieve CA certificates and enroll devices with a
		   compatible SCEP server.
		 https://github.com/certnanny/sscep/
		 John Marrett <johnf@zioncluster.ca>

	config PACKAGE_static-neighbor-reports
		tristate "static-neighbor-reports........ Configure static 802.11k neighbor reports"
		default y if DEFAULT_static-neighbor-reports
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_lua
		select PACKAGE_libubus-lua
		select PACKAGE_libc
		select PACKAGE_libuci-lua
		help
		 Allows to configure static neighbor reports for hostapd interfaces.
		 
		   These neighbor reports are avilable to clients using IEEE 802.11k.
		 David Bauer <mail@david-bauer.net>

	config PACKAGE_stunnel
		tristate "stunnel.................................................. SSL TCP Wrapper"
		default y if DEFAULT_stunnel
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_libopenssl
		select PACKAGE_libpthread
		select PACKAGE_zlib
		select PACKAGE_libc
		help
		 Stunnel is a program that allows you to encrypt arbitrary TCP
		 	connections inside SSL (Secure Sockets Layer) available on both Unix
		 	and Windows. Stunnel can allow you to secure non-SSL aware daemons and
		 	protocols (like POP, IMAP, LDAP, etc) by having Stunnel provide the
		 	encryption, requiring no changes to the daemon's code.
		 http://www.stunnel.org/
		 Florian Eckert <fe@dev.tdt.de>

	config PACKAGE_switchdev-poller
		tristate "switchdev-poller......... Poll switchdev ports to bring CPU ports up/down"
		default y if DEFAULT_switchdev-poller
		default m if ALL
		select PACKAGE_libc
		select PACKAGE_swconfig
		help
		 This service monitors switchdev ports and brings down CPU ports when
		   all related non-CPU vlan ports are also down. Otherwise, it brings
		   the port up.
		 Luiz Angelo Daros de Luca <luizluca@gmail.com>

	config PACKAGE_tac_plus
		tristate "tac_plus............................ TACACS+ daemon (without PAM support)"
		default y if DEFAULT_tac_plus
		default m if ALL
